      "apart_run_counts": "The key-check calls a cell reproduced when a run of another lineage gives the key's answer and no rule 2 reason holds, whatever a run that stands apart answers (docs/coverage.md rule 3; reproduction_scope says why the other run stands apart). crosscheck calls the cell contested while a run of another lineage disagrees, unless a closed ledger entry names that run in who_errs.",
      "apart_runs_without_agreement": "Where runs of another lineage answer, none gives the key's answer and no entry disputes the key, the key-check leaves the cell resting on one model (docs/coverage.md rule 4). crosscheck calls it contested: a run of another lineage disagrees and no closed ledger entry sets it aside.",
      "borrowed_input_lineage": "crosscheck joins two runs' lineages where one takes an input that the other computed, unless the binding says the input does not bear on the answer (crosscheck.lineage); bindings.csv names no quantity for the input, so the join holds for every quantity of the case. The key-check joins runs only on a shared engine, convention file or input-map file (scripts/make_cell_status.py lineage_groups) and marks a reproduction that rests on the key run's state and local tax amount instead (status_detail key_salt_amount_itemized, on the income tax lines only).",
