  "schema_gaps": [
    "Not stated: Value.producer. answers.csv does not say which values the model produced and which code outside the model computed, so every value carries 'not_stated'.",
    "Stretched: answers.csv unexpressed_facts becomes Binding.facts_not_taken, but the key-check's README defines the column more widely (facts a model took with a side effect, and readings of unstated facts the answer rests on, as well as facts it could not take), and the key-check also writes scope notes there for rows a model does not cover.",
    "Stretched: runs.csv conventions is prose that describes the conventions and settings a run applied; Run.convention_files holds the whole text as one entry, so lineage reads each distinct text as one convention file, and a text that says no convention applies still yields a convention token.",
    "Stretched: Binding.input_map_author_kind holds one kind, while the key-check's input_map_author text can name several authors in several roles (who wrote the map, who reviewed it, who applied fixes). The exporter writes ai_model when the text names an AI model and unknown otherwise; it never infers a person from the text.",
    "Derived: runs.csv period. Run has no policy world field, so the exporter keeps the period only on the run's values and bindings (as the policy world us.<period>) and project_runs reads it back from them.",
    "Derived: runs.csv input_map and input_map_author. Run has no input map field, so the exporter spreads the run-level text over every binding of the run (layers as Binding.input_maps, 'shared from' parts as BorrowedInput, the author as Binding.input_map_author) and project_runs rebuilds them from the run's bindings.",
    "Not on the run: Run.sources holds the source file runs.csv names for the run (with no sha256, which runs.csv does not state) and answers.csv with its sha256; runs.csv, models.csv and bindings.csv, which crosscheck also reads, have no place on the run, so the differential's evidence records their hashes.",
    "Not held: the row order of answers.csv. The table sorts records by key; the differential compares rows by key.",
    "Not held: the row order of runs.csv. The table sorts records by key; the differential compares rows by key.",
    "Not held: the row order of bindings.csv. The table sorts records by key; the differential compares rows by key.",
    "Not held: runs.csv inputs_from_other_runs. A BorrowedInput holds one description of the input (the input_map part that names the lending run, or bindings.csv's own text when bindings.csv is read); the exporter checks that this column names the same lending run, so only its wording is lost.",
    "Not held: runs.csv shares_with_other_runs. crosscheck computes lineage from engines, convention files, map layers and borrowed inputs, and holds no run's own statement of what it shares with other runs.",
    "Not held: runs.csv input_map, when bindings.csv is read. The bindings give each case's layers and borrowed input, and the run-level text has no field.",
    "Not held: bindings.csv records_sent, model_itemizes, unexpressed_facts, map_computed. The schema has no field for what a binding sent or whether the model itemized, and the notes come from answers.csv without bindings.csv's group tags.",
    "No fitting word: causes.csv kind 'key-decided-value' becomes explained_other, since crosscheck's cause vocabulary has no word for it; LedgerEntry.source_kind keeps the key-check's word.",
    "Not held: causes.csv who_is_right. LedgerEntry.who_errs names the runs judged to err, and the exporter never infers runs from prose, so who_errs stays empty and the entry's position on who is right has no field.",
    "Not held: causes.csv release_or_build, fixed_in, law_figure, evidence. LedgerEntry has no field for where a cause holds, where it is fixed, the figure the law gives or the evidence behind the entry.",
    "Another form: causes.csv answerer and law_years become LedgerEntry.runs (the run of each answerer in each law-year table, as cause_cells.csv pairs answerers with runs); neither the answerer words nor the law-year word comes back as text, and an answerer has no run in a table where cause_cells.csv never pairs it.",
    "Another form: causes.csv quantities and households_shared become ledger cells. A household where every answer moves alike becomes one cell per quantity and law-year table that names no run and predicts no size, so the schema cannot say that the answers there move alike, and the order of the households is not held.",
    "Not held: cause_cells.csv answerer. LedgerCell.run names the run, and the key-check's answerer word, which for the committed key is not a model name, has no field.",
    "Another form: cause_cells.csv amount becomes LedgerCell.predicted_size, a number; the amount's text is not held.",
    "Derived: neither cause table names a case set; each ledger cell takes the one case set of the tables that holds its case in its world.",
    "Not exported: cell_status.csv. crosscheck stores no status (it computes one on read); compare_cell_status sets the key-check's statuses beside crosscheck's."
